Theorem TF-15: Set transfer produces no dst (in-place mutation; row "—")

  Preconditions:
    - Instruction is `Set { base, field, value }` per Annex E §AIMS
      TF-15 + Appendix A row 14
    - `Set` performs in-place mutation of `base.field := value`; no
      destination variable is defined
    - Appendix A row 14 carries "—" across every per-dimension column —
      no forward transfer (the instruction defines no SSA value)
    - Backward demand `(base, Once)` + `(value, Once, Linear)` is proven
      at §04.3 TF-11 (standard backward demand)
    - IA-5 step (1) intraprocedural alias-transfer (`value.access := Owned`
      unconditional + `value.locality := max(value.locality, base_state.locality)`)
      is proven at §04.3 IA-5-step-1 — §04.2 TF-15 cites the anchor and
      proves the no-dst forward-row property

  Soundness property:
    Forall Set { base, field, value }.
      transfer_tf15(Set) = NoDst (no AimsState emitted)
    AND Appendix A row 14 carries "—" across every per-dimension column.
    L-6 layer (b) monotonicity holds trivially — no output state to
    monotone over (no codomain element to compare).

  Proof obligation:
    Three-part discharge:
      (a) No-dst confirmation — verify TF-15 emits NoDst (the "—"
          marker in Appendix A row 14). The state map MUST NOT acquire
          a new entry from this instruction.
      (b) Per-dimension "—" verification — every Appendix A row 14
          column reads "—" verbatim (no Access / Consumption /
          Cardinality / Uniqueness / Locality / Shape / Effect emitted).
      (c) L-6 layer (b) monotonicity — vacuously holds for no-dst
          instructions: the forward-transfer codomain is empty, so the
          monotonicity quantifier ranges over an empty set. Any pair
          (a, b) of input states with a ≤ b satisfies the (vacuous)
          property "f(a) and f(b) are comparable on the dst codomain"
          since there is no dst codomain element.

    Part (a) — no-dst confirmation:
      Per Annex E §AIMS TF-15: "Set { base, field, value }: in-place
      mutation, no `dst`. No forward transfer."
      Verified: transfer_tf15() returns a NoDst marker (not Tagged::State,
      not Tagged::Scalar). The state map MUST be UNCHANGED by Set
      execution (modulo intraprocedural alias-transfer step (1) on
      `value`'s state — proven at IA-5-step-1 below, NOT part of TF-15
      forward transfer).

    Part (b) — Appendix A row "—" verification:
      Appendix A row 14 columns reads:
        Access: —
        Consumption: —
        Cardinality: —
        Uniqueness: —
        Locality: —
        Shape: —
        Effect: —
      Verified: TF-15 enumeration emits no per-dimension column;
      consistent with the "—" marker. The marker indicates "this
      instruction defines no SSA value" — distinct from emitting
      SCALAR (which IS a value, just with no RC consequence).

    Part (c) — vacuous monotonicity:
      L-6 layer (b) monotonicity is the property:
        forall a, b in AimsState. a ≤ b implies f(a) ≤ f(b).
      For no-dst instructions, `f` has empty codomain — there is no
      `f(a)` value to compare. The implication is vacuously true: any
      property quantified over an empty set holds trivially.
      Cross-reference: backward-demand monotonicity (TF-11 emits
      `(base, Once)` + `(value, Once, Linear)`) is the operational
      L-6 layer (b) for Set; that is proven at §04.3 TF-11. The IA-5
      step (1) intraprocedural alias-transfer (`value.access := Owned`
      + `value.locality := max`) is proven at §04.3 IA-5-step-1.
      §04.2 TF-15 proves only the no-dst forward-row property.

    Engines dispatched:
      monotonicity (PRIMARY — vacuous L-6 layer (b) discharge for
        no-dst instructions per section_04::verify_tf15_set_no_dst)
      case_analysis (PRIMARY — Appendix A row 14 "—" enumeration per
        section_04::verify_tf15_set_no_dst)
      lattice (SECONDARY — accepts gracefully; no codomain element)
      refinement (SECONDARY — accepts gracefully; TF-15 emits no dst,
        no refine() applicable)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_04 monotonicity + case_analysis engines discharge TF-15 via no-dst confirmation + Appendix A row 14 per-dimension "—" enumeration + vacuous L-6 layer (b) monotonicity
